.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt EVP_MD4 3ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm EVP_md4
.Nd MD4 For EVP
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In openssl/evp.h
.Ft const EVP_MD *
.Fo EVP_md4
.Fa void
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
MD4 is a cryptographic hash function standardized in RFC 1320 and
designed by Ronald Rivest, first published in 1990. This implementation
is only available with the legacy provider.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It EVP_md4()
The MD4 algorithm which produces a 128-bit output from a given input.
.El
.Sh NOTES
Developers should be aware of the negative performance implications of
calling this function multiple times and should consider using
.Xr EVP_MD_fetch 3
with
.Xr EVP_MD-MD4 7
instead.
See
.Xr crypto 7
for further information.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
These functions return a
.Sy EVP_MD
structure that contains the implementation of the message digest.
See
.Xr EVP_MD_meth_new 3
for details of the
.Sy EVP_MD
structure.
.Sh CONFORMING TO
IETF RFC 1320.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr evp 7 ,
.Xr provider 7 ,
.Xr EVP_DigestInit 3
